From f820e547fa588e60fb211fce061250dcdbb6c06e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emergent-agent-e1 <github@emergent.sh>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:04:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(private-mode): field-confirmation timestamp robustness +
 new-cycle state reset

Field test 18.09.2026 (FMC130 781479): Air Console showed 'Privatemode ON/OFF' and AVL16
recorded 1.16 km (session CLOSED DEGRADED, correct), yet backend stayed UNKNOWN/TIMEOUT.

ROOT_CAUSE (confirmation): _device_response_confirm read the entry instant ONLY from
e.get('time'). Navixy history can carry it in get_time (as elsewhere in this codebase:
track points, odometer_calibration, beacons). With time absent, _parse(None)=None and the
anti-stale filter dropped EVERY real response -> PR#8 hardware-ACK matcher never reached ->
UNCONFIRMED. FIX: new _entry_time() reads time|get_time|timestamp|event_time (tz-aware);
_device_response_confirm uses it. Anti-stale stays strict (no usable ts / older than
command_sent_at -> refused; success False/error -> never; wrong mode -> refused). Telemetry
fallback unchanged.

FIX 2 (state reset): a NEW PRIVATE cycle now explicitly purges the previous cycle's
end/result fields (private_end_time/odometer, private_distance_km, odometer_end_candidate_km,
end_candidate_sample_at, business_command_sent_at, confirmation_source, requested_target,
last_command, command_sent_at, navixy_command_id, old gps anchor) BEFORE writing the new
START. private_start_* + fresh anchor preserved through PRIVATE->BUSINESS. private_mileage_session
history untouched (1.16 km kept).

+9 field/get_time tests, +2 state-reset tests. Confirmation 35/35, phase2 28/28, full
regression 165/165 PASS (testing_agent). DEVICE_WRITE stays 0; no device command (all mocked).
Adds READ-ONLY diagnostic diagnostics/navixy_confirmation_diag_781479_0918.py.
